From: ksooo <kai.sommerfeld@gmx.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:20:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [ActiveAE] Fix clock unit of visualization data timing

Since e04eae51d1 the current time used to schedule visualization data is
in steady_clock ticks (nanoseconds), while the output delay and the
buffer timestamps are in milliseconds. The delay is thus effectively
ignored and visualizations receive audio data ahead of playback by the
whole output delay, which is especially noticeable with the large
AudioTrack buffers on Android.
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
index 07446ea..7b9e6fb 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
@@ -2610,7 +2610,9 @@ bool CActiveAE::RunStages()
               CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "ActiveAE::{} - viz ran out of free buffers", __FUNCTION__);
             AEDelayStatus status;
             m_stats.GetDelay(status);
-            int64_t now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch().count();
+            int64_t now = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(
+                              std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch())
+                              .count();
             int64_t timestamp = now + status.GetDelay() * 1000;
             busy |= m_vizBuffers->ResampleBuffers(timestamp);
             while(!m_vizBuffers->m_outputSamples.empty())
-- 
